Status: IN_PROGRESS
GitHub issue: https://github.com/Zanark/BowserBoy/issues/87
Milestone: Pick up the side stylus and draw with a camera-facing pen.
Dependencies: 79 separate DS; 87 DS orientation; 88 precise touchscreen input.
Purpose: Make the physical side stylus glow on hover and usable as a pen without
covering the lower LCD with a long sideways shaft.

Tasks:
- [x] Trace existing model, pointer routing, pose bounds and native touch input.
- [x] Add isolated hover glow and pickup of the docked stylus.
- [x] Keep the held nib under the pointer with the back facing the camera.
- [x] Preserve direct LCD input, pose framing and real blur/cancel cleanup.
- [x] Move gameplay hints to one bottom-left line instead of over the play area.
- [x] Qualify native drawing, return controls, orientations and phone-sized input.
- [x] Update affected documentation, tracking and owned continuity.
- [ ] Owner visual/device review.

Acceptance criteria:
The actual side stylus glows on hover without changing lime console buttons.
Click/tap picks it up; its nib stays at the pointer while the shaft points
toward the camera. Drawing uses unchanged physical LCD UVs, respects lid/body
occlusion, and remains correct when rotated, zoomed or resized. Escape,
right-click or Put back returns it; blur, cancellation, modal tools, console
and view changes safely release input and dock it. Direct mouse/touch drawing,
GBA behavior, lighting, paint, saves and the frozen book remain unchanged.
Gameplay hints stay on one bottom-left line, with ellipsis on narrow screens.

Completion evidence:
Syntax,35units and build pass. Final five-case Edge feature gate passes1.6m,
including native pen drawing and tip projection, back facing the camera,
Escape/right-click/keyboard/Put back, cancellation, modal/view/system cleanup
and upside-down390x844DPR2touch. Hint layout passes1440/390/320px.
Actual desktop/phone pen captures reviewed. Owner/device acceptance remains open.

Completion log:
2026-11-07: Owner supplies a pen-over-DS reference and requests hover glow,
pickup and a camera-facing back that does not obscure the screen. Reuse
native touch routing; isolate stylus materials from shared lime controls.
Keep dock geometry in framing bounds and move only the non-pickable held
visual, so pen motion cannot change the gameplay camera or block its own ray.
2026-11-07: Regression exposes shared GBA Escape handling opening DS tools
before the pen can return. Preserve shared move/popover precedence, then let
the DS controller own Escape. Final native pen case passes22.8s; no UV offset.
